{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall take, and the priest shall put.</b> Just as the putting is by the priest himself, so too the taking is by the priest himself. One might think that also the putting upon the altar should be done by hand — Scripture says, ״כי כחטאת האשם הוא לכהן״ (for like the sin-offering, the guilt-offering belongs to the priest): just as the sin-offering requires a vessel, so too the guilt-offering requires a vessel. You conclude that two priests receive his blood — one in a vessel and one by hand; and this one who received in a vessel comes and dashes it on the wall of the altar, and this one who received by hand comes to the metzora."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:11.385835616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}